Give every gsa.apple.com request its own URLSession, and therefore its own connection.

Apple's edge in front of gsa.apple.com serves at most two requests per connection and
answers the rest with HTTP 429. ALTAppleAPI.sharedAPI keeps one ephemeral URLSession for
the app's lifetime, and .ephemeral still reuses keep-alive connections, so signing in
(init -> complete -> apptokens) failed at `complete` every time.

Verified on Apple's own URLSession stack, three POSTs to GsService2, two trials each:
  shared session (build 155):  init=200  complete=429  apptokens=429
  one-shot sessions (156):     init=200  complete=200  apptokens=200

Mirrors rileytestut/AltSign#52. Also moves the four 2FA requests (trusted-device and SMS,
request + verify) off the shared session, since they hit the same host. 2FA does not rely
on cookies carried between those requests: isideload's client has no cookie store at all and
upstream's 2FA works. developerservices2.apple.com calls keep the shared session.
Shipped in OTA build 156. Apply from the repo root with: git apply patches/<this file>

